description:
## Feature Request

It would be great if `desc` had capabilities to **add system requirements** to the DESCRIPTION file. 

Even better would be a way to ensure that the sysreq is compatible with the [rstudio/r-system-requirements](https://github.com/rstudio/r-system-requirements) database and, if not found in the database an encouraging message to add it to the sysreq db. 

Inspired by Posit Package Manager build issue with extendr packages: https://github.com/extendr/rextendr/issues/457

## Motivation 

In `{rextendr}` we add `"Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc >= 1.65.0"` with a custom function that's a little scary (below). ([source](https://github.com/extendr/rextendr/blob/main/R/setup.R))

This function will not effectively handle adding `xz` as a system requirement to existing DESCRIPTION files

```r
update_description <- function(field, value, desc_path) {
  cli::cli_alert_info("Setting {.var {field}} to {.str {value}} in the {.file DESCRIPTION} file.")
  desc::desc_set(field, value, file = desc_path)
}

update_sys_reqs <- function(desc_path) {
  cur <- "Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc"
  prev <- stringi::stri_trim_both(desc::desc_get("SystemRequirements", file = desc_path)[[1]])

  if (is.na(prev)) {
    update_description("SystemRequirements", cur, desc_path = desc_path)
  } else if (!identical(cur, prev)) {
    cli::cli_ul(
      c(
        "The SystemRequirements field in the {.file DESCRIPTION} file is already set.",
        "Please update it manually if needed."
      )
    )
  }
}
```

I've just made a typo in a function I was writing and set "description" instead of "Description". I'm now wondering whether it'd make sense for `desc` to have a list of possible fields and to error (or a list of most classifical fields, including regexp such as starting with "X-schema.org-").

So this below would either get an error or warning or message:
``` r
descr <- desc::desc("!new")
descr$set(notafield = "blabla")
descr
#> Package: {{ Package }}
#> Title: {{ Title }}
#> Version: 1.0.0
#> Authors@R (parsed):
#>     * Jo Doe <jodoe@dom.ain> [aut, cre]
#> Maintainer: {{ Maintainer }}
#> Description: {{ Description }}
#> License: {{ License }}
#> URL: {{ URL }}
#> BugReports: {{ BugReports }}
#> Encoding: UTF-8
#> LazyData: true
#> notafield: blabla
```

<sup>Created on 2018-10-04 by the [reprex package](https://reprex.tidyverse.org) (v0.2.1)</sup>

Or maybe it doesn't make sense because one _can_ set any field in a DESCRIPTION. 🤔

Something like:

``` R
get_one <- function(key) {
  fields <- self$get(key)
  if (length(fields)  != 1) {
   stop(length(fields), " fields, not one", call. = FALSE)
  }

  fields[[1]]
}
```

Maybe `get_value()`? Or `get_single()`?
